WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.250
Hi, My name is Ayush
Sharma, and I'm

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.750
majoring in computer science.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.480
And my work is called
"Privacy Email."

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.780
So companies and organizations
are collecting more of our data

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.310
than ever before.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:16.650
We have tried ways of
privatizing the data by naive

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:19.350
techniques, such as
redacting the sensitive info,

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.570
something called key anonymity.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.400
These techniques
over time have been

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.980
shown to not be very
effective and in fact are

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.510
quite easily breakable.

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:29.910
The golden standard for
privacy is called something

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:31.830
called differential privacy.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:35.310
So consider two data
sets that are neighboring

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:38.520
such that there's one user
present in the data set

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.230
that's not in the other one.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.420
The intuitive notion
of differential privacy

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:46.500
is that what's the difference
of privacy of this user by being

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.260
in the data sets versus
not being in a data set,

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.270
and can you optimize for that?

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:54.270
This is where our work comes
in, because there is currently

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.520
no framework or
library that can use

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:00.000
this technique of differential
privacy for an enabled data

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.370
analysts to use it
in their own work.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:05.760
In "Privacy Email,"
we provide a library

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.420
a tool box where data
analysts can simply

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.450
ask for their parameters
to be set and then

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:16.150
choose the noising mechanisms to
achieve the result of privacy.

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:19.170
What happens that you start
with the sensitive data, can

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:20.790
run the black box
algorithm, which

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:23.430
is written by the
analyst, get the result,

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:27.810
and then we will add the
sensitive noise to the data

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.280
and get the private result.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.610
Bear in mind that we can control
the amount of privacy here

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:35.010
and the epsilon parameter
of the privacy budget.

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:38.260
And this all works seamlessly
with existing infrastructure

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.350
written in Spark
and [? Scala. ?]

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:43.110
In terms of results, we
notice that we can generate

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:47.490
linear regression results and
can get a plus in distribution

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:49.602
from the result as expected.

00:01:49.602 --> 00:01:51.060
And we were able
to quite narrow it

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:55.200
down and provide better utility
without having much overhead.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.472
Thank you.

